[size=5][b]Why SkTestLab?[/b][/size]

A successful reload is a useful start. Repeatable tests help you check the behavior behind your scripts: reward calculations, boundary values, expected failures, and the functions you change most often.

Keep [b].sk[/b] files and [b].sktest.json[/b] tests together in your project. Run a check from VS Code's native Test Explorer, inspect the evidence, and rerun failures while you work.

[size=4][b]A real function. An explicit expectation.[/b][/size]

From the included Reward Lab example, [b]reward.sk[/b]:


[code]
function labReward(tasks: number, multiplier: number) :: number:
    if {_tasks} < 0:
        return 0
    if {_multiplier} < 0:
        return 0
    set {_coins} to floor({_tasks} * 10 * {_multiplier})
    if {_coins} > 1000:
        return 1000
    return {_coins}
[/code]



Save this runtime test beside it as [b]reward-check.sktest.json[/b]:


[code]
{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "reward-check",
  "name": "Five completed tasks earn 50 coins",
  "mode": "runtime",
  "targets": ["reward.sk"],
  "timeoutMs": 300000,
  "actions": ["set {_reward} to labReward(5, 1)"],
  "assertions": [
    { "condition": "{_reward} is 50", "message": "Expected 50 coins" }
  ]
}
[/code]



Configure Runtime, then run it from Test Explorer. Keep [b].sk[/b] and [b].sktest.json[/b] files together in version control, so the behavior you expect travels with your script.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]🔎 Diagnostics while you write[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Twelve configurable diagnostic rules with confidence labels.
[*]Targeted Quick Fixes and cross-file declaration warnings.
[*]Analyze a file or workspace from the Command Palette.
[*]Works alongside your existing syntax-highlighting extension.
[/list]

[size=4][b]⚡ Offline checks[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Assert diagnostics, declared symbols, source text, and structure.
[*]Run without Minecraft, server JARs, or Java.
[*]Versioned [b].sktest.json[/b] definitions, JSON Schema, and snippets.
[*]Generate starting expectations from declarations and review them before use.
[/list]

[size=4][b]🧪 Real Paper/Skript execution[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Select your compatible Paper/Skript JARs and Java executable.
[*]Invoke project functions and evaluate Skript conditions in console context.
[*]Disposable server environments, loopback networking, and owned-directory cleanup.
[*]Observed runtime versions and console evidence retained with results.
[/list]

[size=4][b]▶️ Native VS Code workflow[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Discover and organize tests in Test Explorer.
[*]Run selections, related-file tests, or an entire suite.
[*]Rerun failures, cancel execution, and inspect assertion differences.
[*]Project setup, test generation, analysis, and runtime validation commands.
[/list]

[size=4][b]📊 Results, history, and reports[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Searchable results, filters, sorting, and expandable assertion evidence.
[*]Source links, console excerpts, workspace history, and runtime readiness checks.
[*]Trends for comparable test selections and slowest-test insights.
[*]Export JSON, HTML, or JUnit reports; use the offline CLI for scripted checks.
[/list]

[size=5][b]🎨 Your dashboard, your style[/b][/size]

Choose [b]White[/b], [b]Dark[/b], or [b]Follow VS Code[/b]. Your appearance choice is remembered.

Search, filter, and sort results; expand assertion details; inspect runtime readiness; and follow trends for comparable test selections. Passing, failing, skipped, cancelled, and errored outcomes stay distinct, so incomplete runs do not become a misleading green result.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Alexpetkanov13/SkTestLab/main/docs/images/dashboard-dark.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Alexpetkanov13/SkTestLab/main/docs/images/dashboard-white.png[/img]

[size=5][b]🎁 Included example: Reward Lab[/b][/size]

Start with a small reward calculator written in ordinary Skript. Its tests check normal rewards, invalid inputs, rounding, and the reward cap, with [b]seven real runtime assertions[/b] and an offline source check.

[b]No addons or automated players are needed for the example.[/b]

The download contains [b]the SkTestLab extension and the Reward Lab example[/b].

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download [url=https://github.com/Alexpetkanov13/SkTestLab/releases/download/v1.0.0/sktestlab-1.0.0-skunity.zip]the extension and example ZIP[/url] and extract it.
[*]In VS Code, open [b]Extensions → … → Install from VSIX[/b] and select the included extension.
[*]Extract [b]reward-lab.zip[/b] and open its [b]reward-lab[/b] folder in VS Code.
[*]Run the example's offline test from Test Explorer, then use [b]SkTestLab: Open Dashboard[/b] to inspect the result.
[*]For real server tests, run [b]SkTestLab: Configure Runtime[/b], select your local Java and compatible Paper/Skript JARs, accept the Minecraft EULA, and run the runtime example.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Editor[/b] — VS Code 1.96 or newer
[*][b]Desktop[/b] — Windows x64
[*][b]Offline checks[/b] — No Minecraft server or Java required
[*][b]Runtime server[/b] — Compatible Paper for Minecraft 1.21+
[*][b]Skript[/b] — Verified minor lines 2.9–2.17; choose a release compatible with your Paper version
[*][b]Java[/b] — Java 21.0.12 used for recorded pairings; follow the requirements of your selected Paper release
[*][b]Runtime setup[/b] — Trusted workspace, local Java and JARs, Minecraft EULA acceptance
[/list]

Server and plugin JARs are obtained separately.

[size=5][b]Testing and compatibility[/b][/size]

Ten exact Paper/Skript combinations passed seven Reward Lab assertions each, using Paper 1.21, 1.21.4, or 1.21.11 and Java 21.0.12. The badges summarize this scope; they do not certify every patch pairing. Newer servers may need a different Java version. Other combinations and addons need local verification. Linux, macOS, and Windows ARM64 are not certified for this release.

Release verification also includes [b]166 unit tests[/b], extension-host and distribution checks, and real runtime checks for failing assertions, parser errors, warning-only scripts, cancellation, and cleanup. See the [url=https://github.com/Alexpetkanov13/SkTestLab/blob/main/docs/verification.md]verification record[/url] for the scope and recorded evidence.

[url=https://github.com/Alexpetkanov13/SkTestLab/blob/main/docs/compatibility.md]View the exact tested pairings[/url]

[size=5][b]Useful commands[/b][/size]

Open the Command Palette and search for [b]SkTestLab[/b]:

[list]
[*][b]Initialize Project[/b] and [b]Create Test[/b] to get started.
[*][b]Analyze Current File[/b] or [b]Analyze Workspace[/b] for diagnostics.
[*][b]Run All Tests[/b], [b]Run Failed Tests[/b], and [b]Stop Tests[/b] for execution.
[*][b]Configure Runtime[/b] and [b]Validate Runtime Environment[/b] for server setup.
[*][b]Open Dashboard[/b], [b]Open Test Logs[/b], and [b]Export Test Report[/b] for results.
[/list]

